<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/andorra"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Andorra.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Andorra</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Andorran women gain the vote</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/south-yemen"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/South%20Yemen.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>South Yemen</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The country is renamed the People’s Democratic Republic of Yemen</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-tonga"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Tonga.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Tonga</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Tonga regains full independence and joins the Commonwealth</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/igbo-ukwu-culture"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Igbo-Ukwu%20culture.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Igbo-Ukwu culture</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Shaw publishes radiocarbon dates placing the sites in the 9th century</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/syrian-arab-republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Syrian%20Arab%20Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Syrian Arab Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Hafez al-Assad, Minister of Defense, deposes Salah Jadid in the bloodless Corrective Movement and becomes the state's strongman.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/rhodesia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Rhodesia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Rhodesia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 2 March Rhodesia declares itself a republic after a referendum of 1969 severed the last ties with the Crown by 61,130 votes to 14,327.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-cambodia-1953-1970"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Cambodia%20(1953-1970).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Cambodia (1953-1970)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A coup headed by Prime Minister Lon Nol ends the monarchy and establishes the Khmer Republic</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-vietnam"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Vietnam.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Vietnam</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The government begins the Land-to-the-Tiller program of land reform, limiting individual landholdings to 15 hectares</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/american-indian-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/American%20Indian%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>American Indian Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On Thanksgiving Day an AIM group seizes the replica of the Mayflower in Boston, and AIM declares Thanksgiving a National Day of Mourning</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/black-consciousness-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Black%20Consciousness%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Black Consciousness Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Steve Biko, Barney Pityana, Mapetla Mohapi, Mamphela Ramphele and Bennie Khoapa establish the Black Community Programmes as self-help groups</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/baathism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ba'athism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ba'athism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Corrective Revolution puts Hafez al-Assad in power in Syria</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/native-american-church"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Native%20American%20Church.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Native American Church</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Controlled Substances Act prohibits the possession of psychedelics such as peyote in the United States</span></li></ul></section>
